  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds 64 bars as one instanced box node on a 24×24 floor, in a ring of radius 4. The typecheck passes. I couldn't run the scene (no shell or browser), so the rendering, shadows and camera motion are untested. I also didn't run `vite build`.\n\n- **Heights:** each bar's height comes from four summed sine waves, and the transforms are updated every frame with `setInstances`.\n- **Colour:** each bar has its own colour from an HSL hue gradient around the ring, converted to hex because `hsl()` strings aren't parsed. The colours are passed on every `setInstances` call, as the docs require.\n- **Lighting:** a neutral environment, a hemisphere light, and a shadow-casting directional light, so the bars cast shadows onto the floor.\n- **Camera:** an orbit camera with `interactions.orbit({ autoRotate: 0.15 })`, which should turn it slowly around the ring.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the first `requestAnimationFrame` after `app.ready()`.\n\n",
